Knightlymuse  posted 06-25-2001 05:35 PM CT (US)      <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>I was doing some nice leveling out in The Overthere. As I have said before It’s an ideal location for a druid. Wide open spaces, lots of MOBs, low agro radius, and great experience. The down side was that every night the Goons would venture out along the path and wipe the floor with all the good races. Often they would be trained to the zones. (You could usually avoid this by hunting close to the Skyfire zone.) The other not so great thing was that there were so many different kinds of mobs. We have the Thorny & Spiked Succulents, Stoneler & Stonegazer Cockatrices, Sarnak Bezerkers & Knights, Sabertooth Lions & Tigers, and the Kunark Rhino’s. Finding multi-mobs of the same type could sometimes be quite the adventure all on its own.<BR>Then I found an interesting article over at Casters realm. title of QUAD-KITING COUGARS FROM LEVEL 35-40 IN ICECLAD<P>I won’t go over everything he said but I’d like to expand on it a bit. The big advantage of Iceclad is that it’s you only have one type of mob to contend with, the Snow Cougar. (There’s also Midnight, a named cougar but he’s really easy to pick out because he’s black and all the other cougars are white.) The back part of the island is like Cougar Highway, it can support several groups hunting plus a few druids quad- kiting. Also this area is train free. TRAIN FREE!!!! Even a quad-kite gone bad will not agro on anyone who happens to walk in your path.<P>The front part of the island is mob free, unless they were pulled there. The basic strategy is to gather up four of these cougars. Pull them to the front of the island along the beach (Another advantage of this is that the island slopes down slightly so others will not be able to see your pulls and grab them away by accident or because they think you are in trouble.)<P>Quad-kiting. I did all of my lvl 38 quad-kiting. (Wisdom 178, Evoc is 110 now) and there are some finer points to this that are not mentioned in any of the guides. For example if you ensnare 4 mobs OF THE SAME TYPE, when they get close to you one will pull off from the group. I suspect there is something in the code that prevents more than three ensnared mobs from beating on you all at once. I’ve had six or seven snared mobs following me at one time (when a pull went very very bad) but when they got close only three would attack. Getting the fourth cougar in with the group takes a bit of practice. I have not tested this theory any place else or with any other creature.<P>Casting regeneration on yourself might seem like a waste of mana and med time but it saved me more than once. The cougars hit pretty dang hard and sometimes you can have two or more beating on you at a time. It’s better to play safe than to have to spend an extra hour getting back all the experience you lost because of a death.<P>The last advantage is a rare drop the Cougar Claw Earrings AC4 +3Str +2Dex. Got 4 of em so far in 3 levels and have sold two for a very nice profit. (PC on Cougar Claw earrings?)<P> <BR>Knightlymuse   posted 06-25-2001 05:37 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>The link didn't make it in the last post, I'll try again here. <A HREF="http://eq.castersrealm.com/playguides/VIEW.ASP?ID=5451" TARGET=_blank>http://eq.castersrealm.com/playguides/VIEW.ASP?ID=5451</A>  <P> <BR>bardonbert   posted 06-25-2001 05:48 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Glad to hear that you're enjoying being a druid so much and that you've found a great place to quad kite.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"> I'll have to check it out with Eklah someday.  <IMG SRC="biggrin.gif" border="0"><BR>Allakhazam says that the going rate for a cougar claw earring is 590 pp. They have one more AC but lack the HP bonus of the ever popular orc fang earring (which Allakhazam says goes for about 110 pp).<BR> <BR>Knightlymuse   posted 06-25-2001 05:49 PM CT (US)          <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Three of my own posts. heheh Well I have a few more tips I'd like to add.<BR>Druids are much more rare out here and so their services are highly sought after. I had to turn down groups all the time. Also had SoW up because just about everyone and their uncle wanted it.<P>Use the 3rd person perspective. F9 is your friend. I would usually ensnare the cougars in first person perspective then switch to third to gather them up in a tight group.<P>You can also practice your fishing skill out there. I got mine from 10 to 85 in just under two levels. Gives you something to do on those long med times.<P>Quad kiting is great experience but sometimes it's a lot funner to partner with a really good fighter. You can heal, buff, SoW, and damage shield them and they can hack away with a constant stream of pulls.<P>I'm sure I forgot to write something but I guess it can wait.
